course: dictionary
lesson: 13516
title: Impatience and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Impatience is a feeling. It means you do not want to wait any longer, or you want something to happen very soon. «She waited with impatience for the bell to ring.» The words tell you she was fed up with waiting and wanted the bell right now.
explain: Impatience is a noun, the thing you feel or show. The describing word is impatient: «He is impatient.» The beginning im- means not, and patient means able to wait calmly, so impatient means not able to wait calmly. Look at the word's parts to help you work out its meaning.
explain: Impatience can also mean eagerness. «The children looked at the parcels with impatience, longing to open them.» Here it is a happy wish, not an angry one. Read the clues around the word: the words waiting, longing and wanting show which meaning fits.
fact: Impatience is a noun, so it is a feeling or a thing you can show.
fact: «Impatience» means being annoyed at having to wait, or a strong wish for something to happen soon.
fact: The opposite of impatience is patience: staying calm while you wait.
fact: In stories, Toad is full of impatience for new adventures, and the Queen of Hearts shows her impatience by shouting «Off with her head!»
fact: Impatience can also mean being easily irritated by people or mistakes.
exercise: «She tapped her foot with impatience while the bus was late.» What does impatience mean here? | Feeling proud of her dancing | Feeling hungry for lunch | Feeling calm and sleepy | *Feeling annoyed at having to wait
exercise: «He wanted to open his birthday present with impatience.» What does impatience show? | Being very tired after the game | Being cross with his friends | *Eagerness, a strong wish to start soon | Being bored of the party
exercise: Which word in «Patience helps you stay calm when you wait» names the opposite of impatience? | wait | *Patience | helps | calm
test: Ellie showed impatience with the slow computer, sighing every time it loaded. What does impatience mean here? | Calm acceptance of the delay | Sleepiness | Joy at a new game | *Annoyance at having to wait
test: Sam was full of impatience to start his new job. What does impatience suggest? | Dislike of his boss | Fear of the job | Tiredness after a long day | *A strong wish for it to start soon
exam: «The teacher's impatience with noisy classes made her snap at the children.» Which meaning fits best? | Happiness at the bell | Calm, patient waiting | A strong wish for the holidays to arrive | *Being easily irritated by people
